   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Aladdin** (1 review): Aladdin runs straight into a Maceo jam, then banter and the midnight countdown [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Reverb**: back after 98 archived shows (1598 days) [4]\n- **Maceo jam/banter/countdown**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Happy New Year**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Auld Lang Syne**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Tighten Up**: back after 70 archived shows (991 days) [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2012-12-31.akg483.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 124 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]\n- **soulive2012-12-31.akg483.flac24**: source not stated; 13 songs; 124 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The Shady Horns joined for most of the night: Ryan Zoidis on saxophones, Eric Bloom on trumpet [1]\n- Chris Loftlin on bass and Jeffrey Lockhart on guitar sat in for Auld Lang Syne and Tighten Up [1]\n- The Shady Horns played most of the night: Ryan Zoidis on saxophones, Eric Bloom on trumpet [2]\n- Chris Loftlin on bass and Jeffrey Lockhart on guitar joined for Auld Lang Syne and Tighten Up [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2012-12-31.akg483.flac16**: taped by corey the groundhog (china_c_a_tATyahooDOTcom); transferred by groundhog; source: akg 483 > V2 > R-44 > WAV (24/96k) [1]. Also: Circulated as shared recording number 275 in the Groundhog 2012 series [1]\n- **soulive2012-12-31.akg483.flac24**: taped by corey the groundhog (china_c_a_tATyahooDOTcom); transferred by groundhog; source: akg 483 > V2 > R-44 > WAV (24/96k) [2]. Also: This is a 24-bit transfer, not meant for burning to CD [2]",
